<GuideLayout
  title="Crochet Blanket Sizes"
  description="Standard crochet blanket dimensions and how to turn your stitch gauge into starting chains and row counts."
  path="/guides/crochet-blanket-sizes/"
  answerFirst="Common crochet blanket sizes range from loveys near 12 inches square to king covers over 100 inches wide. Once you pick a finished size, stitches across = (width in inches ÷ 4) × stitches per 4 inches. A 40 inch blanket at 14 sc per 4 inches needs about 140 stitches."
>
  <h2>Standard sizes</h2>
  <p>
    See the full chart on our <a href="/reference/blanket-quilt-sizes/">blanket & quilt sizes</a> page.
    Popular crochet targets: stroller 30×36 in, throw 50×60 in, twin 66×90 in.
  </p>
  <h2>From gauge to starting chain</h2>
  <p>
    Swatch in the stitch you will use (granny clusters differ from single crochet).
    Enter width, length, and gauge in the <a href="/tools/crochet-blanket-calculator/">crochet blanket calculator</a>.
    Add borders afterward so they do not shrink the center motif area unexpectedly.
  </p>
  <h2>Yarn planning</h2>
  <p>
    After you know the size, estimate yarn with the <a href="/tools/yarn-blanket-calculator/">yarn blanket calculator</a>
    set to crochet. Dense stitches and color changes raise yardage.
  </p>
  <h2>Sources</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><a href="https://www.craftyarncouncil.com/standards">Craft Yarn Council</a></li>
  </ul>
</GuideLayout>
